{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-05(ii): record trip TRP-09104 as a FALSE-ARRIVAL event against driver DRV-09104 — the 'arrived' marker was set at 2026-09-04T07:25:20+08:00 while EV-GPS-09104 placed the vehicle 559.37 m from the pickup pin, and no qualifying in-geofence fix exists anywhere in the trip."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To both parties. The SGD 4.00 no-show cancellation fee charged on trip TRP-09104 is refunded in full to the rider. The fee can stand only if all four conditions of POL-NS-01 hold, and two of them fail on the platform's own measurements. EV-GPS-09104 places the driver's vehicle 559.37 m from the registered pickup pin VEN-BP-180 on every one of its 37 fixes (min_distance_m = mean_distance_m = max_distance_m), with qualifying_fix_count 0 and a longest continuous in-geofence run of 0.0 seconds. The driver was therefore never inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival geofence at or before the 07:25:20 'arrived' event — limb (b) fails — and never accumulated any of the 300-second minimum dwell — limb (c) fails. The trip record's own 'arrived' event and 5.7-minute wait figure cannot repair that: under POL-NS-05 a marker set while the trace puts the driver more than 300 m from the pin is FALSE and does not start the waiting clock, which is recomputed from the first qualifying in-geofence fix; there was none. Because no qualifying in-geofence fix exists anywhere in the trip, POL-NS-05(ii) applies directly: full refund, no driver compensation, and the trip recorded as a false-arrival event — that last is the referral above. The same result follows independently under POL-NS-02 (no qualifying in-radius fix → the driver never arrived) and POL-NS-06 (0-second dwell against a 300-second minimum → the fee is refunded whether or not the rider was present or responded). The driver's argument that the gap between the trip record and the GPS must be escalated under POL-NS-09(b) is rejected: that trigger requires that no clause resolves the conflict, and POL-NS-05 is exactly the clause that resolves it. The remaining POL-NS-09 triggers were checked and do not fire — the confidence floor is not engaged, the citable counters are clean (rider no_show_disputes_30d 0; disputes_with_counterparty_90d 0 on both profiles), and the POL-NS-07 anti-farming test on the driver's trailing-30-day figures (1 termination against 120 completed trips) is nowhere near its thresholds, so no compensation is in issue. On the money itself there is no fare defect: the SGD 4.00 line equals the GREATER of the STANDARD zone-class fee (SGD 4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00), so POL-NS-08(d) is satisfied and the whole contested amount is what is refunded. The wrong-entrance route in POL-NS-03 cannot rescue the charge — it is confined to a driver stationary within 400 m of the pin, and this driver was at 559.37 m — so no pin-ambiguity goodwill arises. The rider's own track (519.46 m from the pin) and the absence of any rider chat message mean POL-NS-04 cannot be run, but that is immaterial, because the refund under POL-NS-05(ii)/POL-NS-02/POL-NS-06 does not depend on where the rider was. Finally, traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-09104-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT); it carries no fact and forecloses any dwell accumulation under POL-NS-06(i), but it does not affect the refund. Neither party's profile was used as a ground of decision."
  },
